; Third-person upper-body yaw correction, DEGREES, per torso animation set.
; The xrMPE pack (meshes\actors\stalker_animation_new.omf) bakes a bladed stance into its torso
; motions: composed through the bone chain the chest bone bip01_spine2 sits 20..42 deg further
; round than the stock sets (stock reference = 7.6 deg), and nothing in the engine takes that
; out, so the actor stands turned off centre. Values below are measured from the omf itself:
; chest heading of <set>_aim_1 minus that stock reference, NEGATED -- bone_yaw turns the actor
; the other way (checked in game, the un-negated table made the twist worse).
; Key = the weapon actor_anim_group, or its numeric animation_slot when it names no group.
; A missing key means no correction. Console var actor_torso_yaw is a global trim on top.
; Empty hands (key 0) is deliberately NOT corrected: vanilla itself holds an off-axis relaxed
; pose there (34.2 deg) and the pack is already closer to centre (29.4).
[actor_torso_yaw]
; slot 1 (pistols) walking/running is measured at 41.4/38.6 -- the SAME chest angle as the rifle
; sets that read straight with no correction; only its idle differs, 35.5 against their 45.0.
; -27.8 (from the same wrong stock-pistol baseline as slot 2) parked the pistols ~30 deg round
; from every rifle, which is what "pistols look to the right" was.
1               = 0.0
                                    ; slightly RIGHT: the pack poses pistols at 35.5 on purpose
; slot 2 (AK-family rifles with no named group -- i.e. no launcher attached) is measured at
; 45.0 deg, EXACTLY the same pose as the named 2_gloff/2_glon sets, which carry no correction
; and read straight in game. -37.3 came from comparing against the stock PISTOL set (7.6);
; the stock slot 2 itself sits at 40.9, so the pack is only 4 deg further round and the old
; value swung the actor far to the right whenever the AK-74 had no GL on it.
2               = 0.0                   ; orig -37.3
; slots 3 (bm16, toz34) and 9 (spas12, winchester) are the SAME compact family as slot 8:
; 27.8 / 24.0 / 28.5 against the rifle sets' 45.0 / 44.5 / 39.7, i.e. 17.2 further LEFT.
; Sprint needs none -- escape_0 is 11.9 here against 15.0 there, no relative lean.
3               = -17.2
3_idle          = -16.0             ; standing idle, shotguns: -8.5 (from -17.2) left the gun ~7.5 deg left of the view (screenshot)
3_relaxed       = 20.0              ; weapon lowered, standing still (relaxed idle): the body sits ~20 deg right of the view, as the RPG's
3_sprint        = 0.0
4               = -17.0             ; RPG standing: the face measured 17 deg left of the view (the barrel, 36, over-turned it); orig 0.0
4_sprint        = 0.0               ; sprint: the escape pose is not turned like the walk
4_idle          = -19.5             ; RPG standing still: -17 left the launcher a little left of the aim, -22 too far right
cr_4            = 0.0               ; RPG crouched: reads straight as it is
4_relaxed       = 20.0              ; RPG lowered, standing still (relaxed idle): the body sits ~20 deg right of the view (screenshot, not measured)
5               = 0.0
6               = 0.0
7               = 0.0               ; orig -21.2
; slot 8 (AKS-74u, saiga12 -- the ones with no actor_anim_group) is baked at 27.8 deg while every
; rifle set sits at 45.0, i.e. 17.2 further LEFT, which is what it looks like in game. The sprint
; needs none: escape_0 is ~15 deg in EVERY set, so there is no relative lean there -- hence the
; explicit _sprint = 0 override (a <key>_<action> line wins over the plain key).
8               = -17.2
8_idle          = -8.5              ; standing idle: with -17.2 the torso sat 8.7 deg right of the view (actor_torso_auto_dbg)
8_relaxed       = 20.0              ; weapon lowered, standing still (relaxed idle): the body sits ~20 deg right of the view, as the RPG's
8_sprint        = 0.0
9               = -17.2
9_idle          = -16.0             ; standing idle, shotguns: -8.5 (from -17.2) left the gun ~7.5 deg left of the view (screenshot)
9_relaxed       = 20.0              ; weapon lowered, standing still (relaxed idle): the body sits ~20 deg right of the view, as the RPG's
9_sprint        = 0.0
10              = -17.2
10_idle         = -16.0             ; standing idle, shotguns: -8.5 (from -17.2) left the gun ~7.5 deg left of the view (screenshot)
10_relaxed      = 20.0              ; weapon lowered, standing still (relaxed idle): the body sits ~20 deg right of the view, as the RPG's
10_sprint       = 0.0               ; SPAS-12 (set 10) sprint: 25.5 bent the torso left; orig 25.5
11              = 0.0               ; orig -22.9
13              = 0.0               ; orig -22.9
; Per-action override: <key>_reload wins over <key> while a reload is playing. The pack's 8_mini
; set (MP5 / AKS-74u / the whole slot-8 family) bakes its reload_0 at 27.8 deg against its own
; idle at 45.0 -- 17 deg, which on screen is the torso swinging left as the reload starts. Every
; other set has reload == idle and needs no line here.
machinegun      = -12.8
machinegun_sprint = 0.0             ; sprint: the escape pose is not turned like the walk
machinegun_relaxed = 20.0           ; weapon lowered, standing still (relaxed idle): the body sits ~20 deg right of the view, as the RPG's
; ---- crouched ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; A "cr_<key>[_<action>]" line wins over "<key>[_<action>]" while the actor is crouched. The pack
; bakes its crouch sets on other angles: the compact family (slots 3 / 8 / 9) against the rifle set
; (cr_torso_2) is 31.9 / 31.9 / 34.6 against 37.9 / 46.3 / 26.0 for idle / walk / run -- 6 deg left,
; 14 left, and 9 to the RIGHT -- so the standing -17.2 over-turned it there (11 deg at rest, 26 in
; the crouch run). value = baked - target, the target being the rifle set in the same state.
; Aimed (aim_0, suffix _zoom): 40.7 against 37.9.
cr_3            = 0.0               ; crouched shotguns read straight as they are; orig -6.0
cr_3_walk       = -14.4
cr_3_run        = 8.6
cr_3_zoom       = 2.8
cr_8            = -6.0
cr_8_walk       = -14.4
cr_8_run        = 8.6
cr_8_zoom       = 2.8
cr_9            = 0.0               ; crouched shotguns read straight as they are; orig -6.0
cr_9_walk       = -14.4
cr_9_run        = 8.6
cr_9_zoom       = 2.8
8_mini_reload   = -17.2
                                    ; so the correction adds to the baked angle, not subtracts

; ---- detector sets -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; effective = baked - value, and LOWER effective reads as LEFT on screen. Target for every line below
; is the idle of the set this one stands in for, so the whole "detector out" state sits where the
; weapon alone would. Transitions must use the SAME target as their idle, or the body swings for the
; length of the gesture and back -- that was the "draw/holster turns left" report.
;   set                baked idle / transition -> target
;   pistol+detector      3.6 / 3.5   -> 27.6 (a trimmed pistol 35.5: the full match rotated the gun
;                                             arm with the chest, so this is deliberately short)
;   6+detector          29.0 / 3.5   -> 49.9 (slot 6 = the bolt, and any long gun that gets here)
;   knife+detector      28.9 / 3.5   -> 50.3 (slot 5)
;   0+detector          28.9 / 19.0  -> 28.9 (empty hands keep the pack's own pose, so only the
;                                             transitions are pulled onto it)
pistol+detector               = 0.0	; user's call: the gun arm rides this correction, so none at all
6+detector                    = -20.9
6+detector_drawdevice         = -46.4
6+detector_holsterdevice      = -46.4
6+detector_drawall            = -37.4
6+detector_holsterall         = -46.4
knife+detector                = -21.4
knife+detector_drawdevice     = -46.8
knife+detector_holsterdevice  = -46.8
knife+detector_drawall        = -37.8
knife+detector_holsterall     = -46.8
0+detector_drawdevice         = -7.7	; vs idle_1 22.7 (was -9.9, measured against the wrong idle)
0+detector_holsterdevice      = -8.9	; vs idle_1 22.7 (was -11.0)

; The "<x>+detector" sets ARE baked far squarer than the weapon sets they stand in for
; (pistol+detector chest = 3.6 deg against the pistol set's 35.5). That is deliberate: with a
; detector in the off hand the pack squares the chest up and aims the gun arm relative to THAT.
; Correcting the chest onto the rifle blade rotated the arm with it -- the whole upper body then
; read as swung right, worse than the lean it was meant to cure. Left at 0 = the pack's own pose.
; If the lean ever needs trimming, it wants a SMALL value dialled in game, not the chest delta.
; orig (all removed): pistol+detector -31.9 / _walk -38.7 / _run -27.2, knife+detector -21.5 /
; _walk -18.2 / _run -20.3, 6+detector -16.0 / _walk -32.4 / _run -11.2, 0+detector -16.1

; Neck yaw correction, DEGREES, same keys as [actor_torso_yaw] (<set> and <set>_<action>), applied
; to bip01_neck. Stock CS puts no callback on that bone at all -- one is installed for this.
; Why a second table: the pack's detector gestures are not a rigid turn of the upper body. Against
; the set's own idle, drawdevice_0 measures 0.0 deg at bip01_spine, 7.7 at spine2 and 29.8 at the
; NECK. A spine1 value can only rotate everything together, so no amount of it reproduces "chest
; where it was, neck round" -- four passes at the torso number changed nothing on screen.
; The HEAD gets no table of its own on purpose: it hangs off the neck and follows it.
; value = (baked_neck - the torso key already applied) - idle_neck
[actor_neck_yaw]
0+detector_drawdevice         = -22.1
0+detector_holsterdevice      = -22.3
pistol+detector_drawdevice    = -1.4
pistol+detector_holsterdevice = -1.4
knife+detector_drawdevice     = 23.8
knife+detector_holsterdevice  = 23.8
6+detector_drawdevice         = 23.1
6+detector_holsterdevice      = 23.1
